<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		Mamono honey (built 2026-09-27). A food on the level of vanilla insect jelly,
		and built the same way: the same parent, the same nutrition, the same joyful
		preferability, the same raw-animal-product shelf. One deliberate difference -
		it never poisons anyone. Vanilla jelly carries `FoodPoisonChanceFixedHuman
		0.02` and this def has no such line at all, because that stat's default is 0
		and a line setting it to 0 would say nothing. That is the plan's
		"foodPoisoningChanceFactor 0": reached by omission rather than by a dead
		field.

		Numbers picked to match Medieval Overhaul's own honey (market value 7, mass
		0.025, nutrition 0.05, stack of 25) rather than vanilla jelly's 8, so a colony
		that runs MO sees one honey behaving the same way whether it came out of our
		bee or MO's own bees. The stack limit is MO's number and not a match for one
		milking: a full milking was 25, exactly a stack, until it was halved to 12 on
		2026-09-29, so a batch now lands as a part-stack.

		A plain vanilla-style `tradeability`, so honey is sellable, and the Medieval
		Overhaul patch stops it being GENERATED as trader stock only in the case where
		MO's own honey is what she makes - a spare jar can always still be sold.

		Art: our own jar, shipped 2026-09-29 - Textures/Things/Item/Resource/PMM_Honey.png,
		from an art drop in the Project Mamono Textures folder. A single texture with
		`Graphic_Single` rather than the stack-of-three piles dragonium wears, because the
		drawing is one jar; give it `_a`|`_b`|`_c` variants and it can move back to
		`Graphic_StackCount`. The arachne's silk stays on vanilla cloth.
	-->
	<ThingDef ParentName="OrganicProductBase">
		<defName>PMM_Honey</defName>
		<label>mamono honey</label>
		<description>Honey gathered from the body of a mamono. Thick, fragrant and impossible to spoil.</description>
		<graphicData>
			<texPath>Things/Item/Resource/PMM_Honey</texPath>
			<graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
		</graphicData>
		<stackLimit>25</stackLimit>
		<socialPropernessMatters>true</socialPropernessMatters>
		<statBases>
			<MarketValue>7</MarketValue>
			<Mass>0.025</Mass>
			<Nutrition>0.05</Nutrition>
		</statBases>
		<ingestible>
			<foodType>AnimalProduct</foodType>
			<preferability>MealFine</preferability>
			<joy>0.08</joy>
			<joyKind>Gluttonous</joyKind>
			<ingestEffect>EatVegetarian</ingestEffect>
			<ingestSound>Meal_Eat</ingestSound>
			<!-- Vanilla jelly's own line, and jelly's reason: worth more as a thing to
			     trade and cook with than as caravan rations. -->
			<lowPriorityCaravanFood>true</lowPriorityCaravanFood>
			<babiesCanIngest>true</babiesCanIngest>
		</ingestible>
		<thingCategories>
			<li>AnimalProductRaw</li>
		</thingCategories>
		<allowedArchonexusCount>150</allowedArchonexusCount>
	</ThingDef>

</Defs>
